{"step_index":116,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:06:19Z","input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_tokens":91862,"output_tokens":2408,"thinking":"Initial hypothesis: APIs are functioning as expected, returning valid JSON data. The next step involves creating thorough documentation. This documentation will encompass a project overview, capabilities, and detailed explanations of each threat engine, including spyware/infostealer detection, antivirus/malware heuristics, and LOLRMM tracking of remote desktop control applications.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# 🛡️ AegisShield EDR - Cyber Process Monitor & Threat Eradicator\\n\\n> **Advanced Real-Time Spyware, Antivirus, Remote Desktop Control, Process Monitor, and Trojan Detection Dashboard**\\n> *Scans your system, identifies threats via multi-vector heuristics and threat intelligence, and kills them with a single click.*\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🌟 Key Features\\n\\n### 1. 🕵️ Spyware & Infostealer Detection\\n* **Keylogger & Hook Inspection:** Scans binary imports and memory hooks for keystroke logging (`SetWindowsHookEx`, `GetAsyncKeyState`, `GetKeyboardState`).\\n* **Screen Scraping & Surveillance:** Detects hidden screen recording APIs (`BitBlt`, `GetDC`) and unauthorized background input capture.\\n* **Infostealer Heuristics:** Matches signatures of notorious credential stealers like **AgentTesla**, **RedLine**, **Vidar**, and LSASS dumpers like **Mimikatz**.\\n\\n### 2. 🦠 Antivirus & Malware Engine\\n* **Pure-Python PE Binary Header Analysis:** Extracts COFF headers, architecture, and section structures without requiring external C extensions.\\n* **Shannon Entropy Analysis:** Identifies crypted, packed, or UPX-obfuscated executables (Entropy > 7.15).\\n* **System Process Masquerading:** Flags processes pretending to be Windows system binaries (e.g. `svchost.exe`, `lsass.exe`, `csrss.exe`) running outside `C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32`.\\n* **Typosquatting Detection:** Detects deceptive names like `svch0st.exe`, `lsasss.exe`, `scvhost.exe`, `taskmngr.exe`, and `dwm0.exe`.\\n* **Suspicious Drop Zones:** Detects and flags executables executing out of `%TEMP%`, `Users\\\\Public`, `Downloads`, or the Recycle Bin.\\n* **LOLBins & Obfuscation Heuristics:** Catches encoded PowerShell (`-enc`, `-encodedcommand`), hidden windows (`-w hidden`), download cradles (`IEX Net.WebClient`), `certutil` downloaders, and ransomware volume shadow deletion (`vssadmin delete shadows`).\\n\\n### 3. 📡 Remote Desktop & RMM Detector (LOLRMM)\\n* **Living Off The Land RMM Tracking:** Automatically discovers 60+ dual-use commercial & open-source remote access \n<truncated 6397 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\thann\\\\Downloads\\\\AntiGravity\\\\SpywareProcessMon\\\\README.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
