{"step_index":122,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:07:08Z","input_tokens":2819,"cache_read_tokens":98516,"output_tokens":4936,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nEnhancements will provide direct control to allow or block processes and IPs from the dashboard, along with an access control rules interface. Email integration will include configurable SMTP settings and options for sending threat reports on demand or automatically. A comprehensive HTML report will be generated with detailed threat information, network session data, and system status.\n\nNetwork intelligence will aggregate network usage data, displaying active processes with their connections, and providing source tracing with geo-IP, ASN, and Whois data. This includes assessing IP reputation by identifying legitimate services and potential threats.\n\n\nConsidering whether the IP is private or a known malicious entity is crucial. Evaluating executable authenticity, checking for digital signatures, and analyzing its location in the file system will inform the IP verdict badge. The user's directive necessitates a structured plan with detailed components and changes, formatted as a markdown artifact for user review.\n\n\nConsidering persistent rule storage for allowlist/blocklist policies, implemented with a JSON file for the initial scope. The API endpoints need definition, including GET, POST, and DELETE methods for rule management. Email integration requires configuring SMTP settings and securely storing them, along with generating HTML reports.\n\n\nExecutive summary will feature a health score, threat count, and network status overview, along with critical/high-threat tables and an audit of active remote sessions. Network intelligence will involve active process socket enumeration and reverse DNS lookups, with geolocation and ASN/ISP lookup incorporating an offline database and public API fallback. The genuineness classifier will categorize IPs based on cloud/CDN provider association, private IP ranges, and known high-risk indicators, correlating process digital signatures for enhanced assessment.\n\n\nConsidering API endpoints for network analytics: aggregating statistics for network processes, open sockets (internal/external), and identifying suspicious endpoints. Examining the design of a detailed connections list that includes IP metadata, geolocation, and a genuineness verdict. Further, incorporating endpoints to trace specific IPs and add firewall block rules.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Comprehensive technical implementation plan for extending AegisShield with:\\n1. Allow & Block Access Control Engine (processes, hashes, and IP addresses)\\n2. Automated & On-Demand Email Reporting System (SMTP with HTML security reports)\\n3. Network Intelligence & Origin Tracer (process network usage, IP geolocation, reverse DNS, and genuineness assessment)\\n4. Interactive Dashboard UI extensions and REST API endpoints\",\"UserFacing\":true}","Content":"\"# 🛡️ Implementation Plan: AegisShield Advanced Features\\n\\nThis plan outlines the architecture, data models, backend engines, and frontend interfaces for the three requested features:\\n1. **Allow / Block Policy Control Engine** (Whitelisting & Blacklisting for Processes & IPs)\\n2. **Automated & On-Demand Email Security Reporting** (SMTP with HTML Incident Reports)\\n3. **Network Intelligence & Origin Tracer** (Process Network Auditing, IP Geolocation, Reverse DNS, and Genuineness Assessment)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 🏗️ Architectural Overview & File Map\\n\\n```\\nSpywareProcessMon/\\n├── backend/\\n│   ├── policy_engine.py       # [NEW] Allow/Block rules engine (process names, paths, hashes, IPs)\\n│   ├── email_notifier.py      # [NEW] SMTP email dispatcher & HTML threat report generator\\n│   ├── network_tracer.py      # [NEW] Network process auditor, IP reverse DNS, GeoIP & Genuineness scorer\\n│   ├── config.py              # [MODIFY] Add database paths for rules, email settings, and geo cache\\n│   ├── detector.py            # [MODIFY] Integrate policy engine (skip allowed, flag/auto-kill blocked)\\n│   ├── remediator.py          # [MODIFY] Support IP firewall blocking & policy enforcement\\n│   └── server.py              # [MODIFY] Expose REST APIs for policies, email dispatch, and network tracer\\n├── database/\\n│   ├── policy_rules.json      # [NEW] Persistent allowlist and blocklist rules\\n│   ├── email_config.json      # [NEW] SMTP server configurations\\n│   └── geo_cache.json         # [NEW] Cached IP geolocation and reputation lookups\\n├── frontend/\\n│   ├── index.html             # [MODIFY] Add Network Tracer, Policy Rules, and Email Settings views\\n│   ├── css/dashboard.css      # [MODIFY] Add styling for genuineness badges, IP tables, and forms\\n│   └── js/app.js              # [MODIFY] UI controllers for network explorer, allow/block actions, email dispatch\\n└── README.md              \n<truncated 8134 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\thann\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\f941cc48-3dd0-4ea9-a4df-91daf625a4db\\\\plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
