{"step_index":126,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:08:00Z","input_tokens":2750,"cache_read_tokens":104326,"output_tokens":3346,"thinking":"Creating the policy engine, starting with rule storage in a JSON file. Initializing match functions for processes and IP addresses based on the specified criteria.\n\n\nThe policy engine's architecture is in place, and now the network tracing component is planned. It will identify and analyze network processes, perform reverse DNS lookups (with caching), and determine geolocation and ASN information. A genuineness scorer will classify connections based on criteria such as cloud/CDN status, private LAN, suspicious ports, and anonymization, returning detailed connection metadata. Integration with the email notifier, detector, and remediator components is planned.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nAegisShield - Access Control & Allow/Block Policy Engine\\nManages whitelisted (trusted) and blacklisted (banned) processes, hashes,\\nand remote IP addresses with optional Windows Firewall integration.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport os\\nimport json\\nimport time\\nimport subprocess\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\\n\\nfrom .config import DATABASE_DIR\\n\\nRULES_FILE = DATABASE_DIR / \\\"policy_rules.json\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass PolicyEngine:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Manages system allowlist and blocklist security policies.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        self._rules = self._load_rules()\\n\\n    def _load_rules(self) -> Dict[str, List[Dict[str, Any]]]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Load persistent rules from database.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        default_rules = {\\n            \\\"allowed_processes\\\": [\\n                {\\n                    \\\"id\\\": \\\"rule_allow_default_1\\\",\\n                    \\\"type\\\": \\\"name\\\",\\n                    \\\"value\\\": \\\"explorer.exe\\\",\\n               